+/* STRIP_INDEXED=1 (opt-in): native strips as an INDEXED draw with D3D's
+ * strip cut (0xFFFFFFFF) in place of RSX primitive restart.
+ *
+ * The native path writes one 256-byte vertex per strip index plus 2-3
+ * repeated vertices at every restart join (degenerate triangles keep the
+ * winding). J-Stars' strips are mostly 3-index pieces + restart, so that is
+ * ~6 vertices per triangle, ~870k per fight frame. Here each DISTINCT guest
+ * vertex of a record is fetched once, the index buffer carries the strip with
+ * a cut at every restart, and the GPU restarts the strip itself. A cut
+ * resets the winding exactly as an RSX restart does, so the triangles drawn
+ * are the same ones the padded strip drew, minus its degenerate joins.
+ * The vertex count drops to the record's distinct vertices; every PSO that
+ * draws VP records gets IBStripCutValue 0xFFFFFFFF (ignored by the
+ * non-indexed draws). */
+#define SIX_CAP (MAX_VP_VERTICES * 2u)           /* u32 indices per parity half */
